To mount your camera on a drop ceiling T-rail, use the included hardware. The hardware can be used to mount to most 9/16", 15/16", or 1 1/2" T-rails.

1. Using the dashed lines on the mount plate template as a guide, set the proper spacing of the clips.


2. Tighten the set screws on the T-rail clips and secure them using a 5/64" (2 mm) hex key.
<PIC:Manual33_11>
{{image description: Mount plate installation template for a Meraki MV21 shown below two T-rail clip positions. Dotted vertical guide lines align the clips with the template, and a bold horizontal arrow spans the template with the note, 'Use these lines to set drop ceiling T-rail clip spacing.' The same mount-type list and labeled holes A through I are visible, along with the Cisco logo and 'Meraki MV21'.}}




3. Attach the mount plate to the T-rail clips using the mount plate holes (marked with a "G").
<PIC:Manual33_12>
{{image description: Line drawing of two mounting clips attached along a ceiling T-rail, with a circular magnified inset showing one clip in detail. A callout label reads 'Set screws' and points to the black screw positions on the clip.}}




4. Attach the T-rail clips to the T-rail by rotating them and snapping them into place as shown. The black foam pads should be compressed slightly after installation.
<PIC:Manual33_13>
{{image description: Exploded line drawing showing two T-rail mounting clips above a camera mounting plate, with dotted vertical alignment lines down to the plate holes and two screws below. The plate has multiple slots, holes, and side hooks for attaching to the clips.}}




<PIC:Manual33_10>
{{image description: Line drawing of a T-rail with two separate mounting clips positioned between upper and lower rail views. Dotted vertical lines and circular arrow symbols indicate the clips are rotated upward into the rail. No text labels are present.}}

